Subject: [PATCH] Negotiate SecP256r1MLKEM768 and SecP384r1MLKEM1024

Apply after boring-pq.patch, boringssl.patch, boringssl-loongarch.patch,
boringssl-windows.patch, and agy-clienthello.patch, against BoringSSL
91a66a59b6c1435120ff83e245d7719411294386. Default group preferences and
ClientHello byte ordering are unchanged.

Implement RFC 10024 sections 4.1-4.3 using the existing EC and FIPS 203
ML-KEM primitives, not the draft Kyber construction. Both groups encode
uncompressed ECDHE || ML-KEM in public shares and ciphertexts, and
fixed-width ECDH x-coordinate || ML-KEM shared secret in the TLS key
schedule. Register them as TLS-1.3-only groups so the existing generic
HelloRetryRequest path generates fresh, real key shares. Wrong sizes,
invalid EC points, and noncanonical ML-KEM public keys are rejected.
Correct-length invalid ML-KEM ciphertexts retain constant-time implicit
rejection and cannot complete TLS record authentication.

The EC helper writes into the final hybrid secret allocation; the ML-KEM
output goes directly into CBB storage. No extra per-component secret
allocation, cryptographic implementation, or production RNG override.
NIDs 972/973 remain reserved by the existing fork's FFDHE definitions;
the object table preserves their previous unregistered status.

Native SSL tests pin each server's only group, force both initial-share
and HRR handshakes, exchange application data, compare both directions
against primitive-level fixed-seed/scalar-one peers, reject malformed
shares, and exercise implicit rejection plus tampered TLS ciphertext.
The normal cryptographic RNG remains active in production code. These
are deterministic test scenarios, not deterministic production keypairs.

References:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc10024#section-4
https://go.dev/src/crypto/tls/key_schedule.go (hybridKeyExchange)

Parent verification (not executed by this patch author):
  cmake --build <native-build> --target ssl_test crypto_test
  <native-build>/ssl_test --gtest_filter='NISTCurves/SSLHybridGroupTest.*:SSLTest.CurveRules:SSLTest.DefaultCurves:SSLTest.ClientHelloAdvertisementsPreserveValidation'
  <native-build>/ssl_test
  <native-build>/crypto_test --gtest_filter='ObjTest.*:MLKEMTest.*'
Then run the Go group-only interop matrix, including HRR, against the
Rust transport before any production cutover.

